01. ISMS Scope

Organisation

Harrow & Lane LLP is a fictional London law firm with 60 employees. It handles confidential legal documents, client financial information and personal data.

The firm uses Microsoft 365, a cloud document management system and an outsourced IT provider.

What is included?

The Information Security Management System (ISMS) covers:

All 60 employees and their work devices.

Microsoft 365, including Outlook, Teams and OneDrive.

The firm's cloud document management system.

Confidential client files and financial records.

Office networks and remote working.

Security risks involving external IT suppliers.

What is excluded?

The internal infrastructure of third-party suppliers is outside the firm's direct control. However, risks arising from those suppliers will still be assessed and managed.

Why this scope?

The firm handles sensitive client information, so protecting confidentiality, integrity and availability is important.

This scope focuses on the people, systems and information most relevant to the firm's legal services.

Project Assumptions

The firm operates from one London office and supports remote working. These details are fictional assumptions used for this exercise.

This is a simulated ISO 27001 project, not an actual certification assessment.
